^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.mem]/1, [temp.variadic]/1: an out-of-line member definition
repeats the class template's template-head, so it defines an ordinary
member when its template-parameter-list has exactly the class template's
parameters; a parameter pack is ONE parameter, however many arguments the
specialization has.  Class-template instantiation compared the
definition's parameter count with the number of ARGUMENTS
(function<int, int, int>: three, against the definition's two), took
`template <class R, class... A> function<R, A...>::function(const
function &)' for a member template and skipped it, so the copy
constructor had no body and the copy read nondet.  The partial
specialization shape (libc++'s `function<R(A...)>') still fails, for a
different reason: cpp11_out_of_line_constructor_template_definition_matched_by_signature.
Fails on the round-163 build bin52.
